# Trimmomatic + Bowtie2 hg38 Mapping Pipeline

## Overview

This O2 pipeline performs:

```text
paired-end FASTQ
    |
    v
Trimmomatic
    |
    v
trimmed paired FASTQ
    |
    v
Bowtie2 mapping to hg38
    |
    v
coordinate-sorted BAM
    |
    v
BAM index + mapping statistics
```

The resulting BAM contains the Bowtie2 alignments without any downstream MAPQ filtering. Filtering can be performed later as needed.

---

## Required O2 modules

The script loads:

```bash
module purge
module load gcc/14.2.0
module load trimmomatic/0.39
module load bowtie2/2.5.4
module load samtools/1.21
```

---

## Inputs

The script takes three command-line arguments:

```text
SAMPLE
R1.fastq.gz
R2.fastq.gz
```

Example:

```bash
sbatch trim_bowtie2_hg38.sh \
    P12a \
    P12a_R1.fastq.gz \
    P12a_R2.fastq.gz
```

---

## Paths to edit

Before running, edit these two variables near the top of the script.

### hg38 Bowtie2 index

```bash
HG38_INDEX="/path/to/Human_Gchr/hg38"
```

This must be the **Bowtie2 index prefix**, not the FASTA file itself.

For example, if the index files are:

```text
/path/to/Human_Gchr/hg38.1.bt2
/path/to/Human_Gchr/hg38.2.bt2
/path/to/Human_Gchr/hg38.3.bt2
...
```

then use:

```bash
HG38_INDEX="/path/to/Human_Gchr/hg38"
```

### Adapter FASTA

```bash
ADAPTERS="/path/to/adapters.fa"
```

Set this to the adapter FASTA appropriate for the sequencing library.

---

## Trimmomatic settings

The script runs paired-end Trimmomatic with:

```text
ILLUMINACLIP:adapter.fa:2:30:10
LEADING:3
TRAILING:3
SLIDINGWINDOW:4:15
MINLEN:36
```

Four FASTQ files are produced:

```text
SAMPLE_R1_paired.fastq.gz
SAMPLE_R1_unpaired.fastq.gz
SAMPLE_R2_paired.fastq.gz
SAMPLE_R2_unpaired.fastq.gz
```

The paired surviving reads are used for Bowtie2 mapping.

The unpaired surviving reads are retained in the output folder but are not mapped by this script.

---

## Bowtie2 mapping

Bowtie2 is run using:

```text
--very-sensitive
```

with the trimmed paired FASTQ files.

The SAM output is streamed directly through `samtools` and coordinate-sorted, so a large intermediate SAM file is not written to disk.

No MAPQ filtering is applied during this step.

---

## O2 resources

The default Slurm request is:

```text
8 CPUs
40 GB RAM
24 hours
```

defined as:

```bash
#SBATCH -c 8
#SBATCH -t 1-00:00
#SBATCH --mem=40G
```

These can be adjusted if needed.

---

## Output

For a sample named:

```text
P12a
```

the output directory is:

```text
P12a_Hg38_BT2/
```

with:

```text
P12a_Hg38_BT2/
├── trimmed/
│   ├── P12a_R1_paired.fastq.gz
│   ├── P12a_R1_unpaired.fastq.gz
│   ├── P12a_R2_paired.fastq.gz
│   └── P12a_R2_unpaired.fastq.gz
│
├── P12a_All_wholeHg38_BT2.bam
├── P12a_All_wholeHg38_BT2.bam.bai
├── P12a.bowtie2.log
├── P12a.flagstat.txt
└── P12a.idxstats.txt
```

The main alignment file is:

```text
P12a_All_wholeHg38_BT2.bam
```

This BAM can subsequently be used for MAPQ filtering, strand separation, repeat AUC analysis, or other downstream analyses.
